NAME
     expr - evaluate one expression

SYNOPSIS
     expr EXPRESSION

DESCRIPTION
     expr evaluates the expression given as its arguments and prints the
     answer: arithmetic (+ - * / %), comparison, the boolean & and |,
     string length, substr, index and match against a regular
     expression. It exists for shell scripts; $((...)) in the shell is
     quicker.

SEE ALSO
     bc(1), sh(1), test in sh(1)
